OL,3,GNEWSAWhy some charity donations do more
OL,4,Aharm than good
OL,5,
OL,6,FJane Ward is turning the blackened,
OL,7,Fmouldy pages of a Mr Men book. "You
OL,8,Fwouldn't want your child curled up in
OL,9,Fbed with this," she says.
OL,11,FWe are at a charity shop run by St
OL,12,FBarnabas Hospice in Lincoln. On the
OL,13,Ftable in front of us is a fleece work
OL,14,Fjacket, covered in dog hair, along with
OL,15,Fa large, stained teddy bear and a
OL,16,Fsingle, dirty, grey slipper.
OL,18,F"If we had the pair, it still wouldn't
OL,19,Fbe wearable," Ward, the store's deputy
OL,20,Fmanager, tells me. "Even our rag
OL,21,Fcompanies wouldn't be able to accept
OL,22,Fthat."
